      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Alcibiades presents a fascinating study in political ambiguity. To view him purely as a realist is to acknowledge his brilliant strategic mind and self-preservation instincts within a chaotic power struggle. However, his frequent betrayal and opportunistic nature strongly suggest a profound moral flexibility, making him a complex figure rather than simply one or the other. Ultimately, he embodies the ruthless pragmatism so often required, yet ethically condemned, by high-stakes ancient politics.",
      "source": "target",
