    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. so if we're looking at it through a historical lens, wouldn't most historians agree that his personal ambition actually caused more harm to Athens than any of his \"brilliant\" moves helped? like, was there even a realistic version of history where he wasn't just a destructive force for the city?",
