      "content": "Many contemporary historians lean towards viewing his ambition as a corrosive force that ultimately destabilized Athenian politics more than his brilliant tactics helped. His actions often prioritized personal renown and influence over the long-term health of the democracy. Given that his shifting loyalties continuously fractured military and political alliances, a consistently \"good\" outcome for Athens seems historically implausible. He remains a prime example of genius corrupted by unchecked self-interest.",
      "source": "target",
